{{WeaponInfoboxAutomatic}}
{{Codex|Cultivate a meaningful relationship with this deceptively simple battery-powered pistol. The Plinx rewards attention and investment from the wise.}}
'''Plinx''' is a [[Corpus]] semi-automatic, battery-powered laser pistol with the ability to auto-refill its ammo passively similar to the {{Weapon|Cycron}}. Possessing excellent [[critical chance]] and [[critical multiplier]] stats, this comes at the cost of a low [[status chance]] and very low ammunition.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage and has innate {{D|Heat}} damage.
*Does not use ammo pickups; ammo regenerates over time.
**Has a '''0.8''' second delay after the weapon stops firing before regenerating ammo. Then, regenerates '''20''' ammo per second; takes '''0.5''' seconds to regenerate a fully depleted battery excluding the delay.

{{Advantages|
*Tied with {{Weapon|Athodai}} for the fourth highest [[critical chance]] of all pistols, behind {{Weapon|Akbolto Prime}}, {{Weapon|Knell Prime}} and a fully charged {{Weapon|Epitaph}}.
*Tied with {{Weapon|Aksomati}}/{{Weapon|Aksomati Prime}} and {{Weapon|Spira Prime}} for the third highest [[critical multiplier]] of all pistols, behind {{Weapon|Nukor}} and {{Weapon|Kuva Nukor}}.
*Very high [[accuracy]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Shots have limited range of '''100''' meters.
*Does not benefit from mods that increase [[Ammo#Ammo Maximum|maximum ammo]], due to lack of an ammo pool.
*Does not receive benefit from reload-triggered mods such as {{M|Pressurized Magazine}}.
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Tenet Plinx}}

==Acquisition==
The Plinx's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Tips==
*Because the 10 shots count as part of a single magazine rather than an ammo pool, mods like {{M|Trick Mag}} have no effect. Magazine increasing mods like {{M|Ice Storm}}, {{M|Slip Magazine}}, or {{M|Tainted Clip}} could be used instead but these mods have far less potency.
**In addition, the recharge rate is also fast enough to the point where increasing this recharge speed and delay has diminishing returns, offering little effect at the cost of a slot.

==Trivia==
*The name likely refers to "plinking," a slang term for recreational target shooting.
*The weapon’s design is most likely modeled after the Derringer type of pistol, known for typically having a small caliber and low ammo capacity, which is reflected in its stats. However, the Lato Prime is more visually similar to the Derringer Pistol in design than the Plinx.
*The Plinx is famously featured during the [[TennoCon/2021]] showcase of [[The New War]], as it is the only available gun to Corpus engineer [[Veso|Veso-R]] who, commenting on the weapon as rather unremarkable, has to equally rely on his command of proxies in order to comply with his superior [[Alad V]]'s orders.
**In the second part of The New War quest itself, the gun indeed gets used by Veso himself.

